A||||5||contra||How can i check problem codes with my fiero??||||1||
Z||000000||contra||08-24-2000||07:33 PM||||i hear you all mention codes being flashed at you when there is a problem. Me being still new to cars and everything, i would like to know how i can see these things too and what kind of equipment i need etc.<BR>thanx<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||08-24-2000||08:26 PM||||Got a Paper clip? it's all you need. All you do i ground a terminal beside the cig. lighter. Pick up a haynes manual you'll need one to know what all the codes mean. you only need to check them if the "Check engine" light is on.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||08-25-2000||03:21 AM||||When looking at the connector next to the cig lighter (panel removed) place paper clip into the 2 top left sockets. Then once grounded turn the car to run (don't start it, just turn until the lights on the dash come on) At this point the check engine light will be flashing. It will flash once, pause then flash twice. This is code 12. A normal condition. It will flash 12 three times then start flashing error codes (3 times each code). All codes are 2 digits. So 3 flashes, pause, 2 flashes is a code 32. Any service manual (Haynes, Chiltons, etc) will have a code listing under the Emissions section. When all the codes have flashed the light will go back to the beginning and flash code 12 again.<BR>If the check engine light comes on while driving and then goes off the error code is still stored in the memory. To clear codes you need to disconnect the battery for a minute or so.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||08-25-2000||05:34 AM||||Here's a link you should add to your favs contra <A HREF="http://www.surf.to/FIERO_OSG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.surf.to/FIERO_OSG</A>  it contains directions for getting and reading the codes as well as MANY other tech directions. Save this one as well <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A> <P>Marc 87GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||08-25-2000||06:14 AM||||If you don't feel comfortable using a paper clip, try Autozone.  Just ask for a GM code key.  They're free if they have any left.  They should have a free booklet, too that will explain what most if not all the codes are.||||reg||1
Z||000005||deceler8||08-26-2000||10:27 AM||||Last time I was at Wal-Mart, they had the GM code readers for $19.99. Just plug it in to your ALDL socket and it does the rest.<P>Paper clip is cheaper, though.||||reg||1
